.shipcheck/
shipcheck-report.md
shipcheck-reply.md
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
server/node_modules/

# the fixture's node_modules is synthetic (stub packages for selftest.py, not
# real installed dependencies) and must be tracked so CI has it on a clean
# checkout -- without it the required-reason/SDK-manifest checks degrade to
# gaps instead of findings and the self-test fails
!examples/bad-expo-app/node_modules/
!examples/bad-expo-app/node_modules/**

# clean-expo-app's node_modules just needs to exist (node_modules_present=True)
# -- no stub packages needed, since nothing in this fixture requires one.
!examples/clean-expo-app/node_modules/
!examples/clean-expo-app/node_modules/**

# but do ship the example report as sample output
!examples/bad-expo-app/shipcheck-report.md
!examples/clean-expo-app/shipcheck-report.md

bindings.json
evals/results/

# Launch/marketing working notes are deliberately NOT published.
# They contain the licence-server failure mode in plain words, live Lemon
# Squeezy discount and product ids, subreddit self-promo ratios, and internal
# notes about other Baker Ventures products -- all of which read very badly to
# someone who finds them from a Show HN link, and none of which a user needs.
# competitive-analysis.md is the deliberate exception: the public
# docs/guidelines/vs-free-claude-code-checkers.html page cites it as its source,
# and its honesty about competitors is a credibility asset.
marketing/*
!marketing/competitive-analysis.md
